        // The locked fractions above are calibrated to a 1.538 fullscreen — on any other shape they
        // slid off-grid: column 1 sliced in half (shifting every fixed-position rune ID), the bottom
        // wrap rows cut off, and at ~20px cells Sonnet can't tell an owned stone from a greyed ghost →
        // it printed a phantom "1" on every unowned rune. For foreign aspects take the WHOLE LEFT 46%
        // at full height (the stash panel is always left-anchored in D2R, any window shape) and upscale
        // HARDER (long edge 2300, cap 4×) so the digits AND the owned-vs-ghost tint survive WhatsApp
